Your repository is not a backup of the CMS. It is the content store.

Structured fields use stable JSON. Long-form text uses Markdoc. Images sit beside the entry that uses them. The same input always produces the same file order, so reviews show the change that matters.

## One publish, one commit

Saves accumulate in a draft workspace where only editors see them. Publish writes everything pending — entries, sidecar files, and media together — as one Git commit. The editor is the author of the commit and Mica is the committer. The self-hosted editor pushes it over HTTPS to any Git host. The local editor commits in your checkout with your own Git.

The self-hosted editor keeps its own clone and syncs it on its own. It fetches the branch and fast-forwards. It never merges.
